---
import { outcomes } from '../lib/landing-content';
import './Outcome.css';
---

<section class="outcome dark-field" id="outcomes" aria-labelledby="outcome-title">
  <div class="outcome-inner">
    <header class="outcome-intro">
      <div>
        <p>What changes</p>
        <h2 id="outcome-title">The team stops being the glue.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Austi is meant to remove routine coordination—not the relationships, policy or judgment that belong to your people.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="outcome-workbench" data-tab-group data-active-tab="0" aria-label="Proposed Austi outcomes">
      <div class="outcome-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Outcome views">
        {outcomes.map((outcome, index) => (
          <button
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            id={`outcome-tab-${index}`}
            aria-controls={`outcome-panel-${index}`}
            aria-selected={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
            tabindex={index === 0 ? 0 : -1}
          >
            <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <strong>{outcome.name}</strong>
            <small>{outcome.detail}</small>
          </button>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="outcome-panels">
        <article class="outcome-panel" id="outcome-panel-0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="outcome-tab-0">
          <header><span>One repair, viewed two ways</span><h3>From scattered handoffs to one case with an owner.</h3></header>
          <div class="coordination-comparison">
            <section class="fragmented-flow" aria-label="Fragmented coordination example">
              <div class="comparison-label"><strong>Without the layer</strong><span>Five separate places</span></div>
              <ol>
                <li><i>IN</i><span><strong>Resident email</strong><small>Leak reported · 22:14</small></span></li>
                <li><i>PH</i><span><strong>Clarification call</strong><small>Notes stay with one person</small></span></li>
                <li><i>WA</i><span><strong>Owner approval</strong><small>Forwarded in a chat</small></span></li>
                <li><i>CO</i><span><strong>Contractor thread</strong><small>Availability needs chasing</small></span></li>
                <li><i>PM</i><span><strong>PMS update</strong><small>Still waiting after the visit</small></span></li>
              </ol>
              <p>The coordinator carries context between every step.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="connected-flow" aria-label="Connected coordination example">
              <div class="comparison-label"><strong>With Austi</strong><span>One operational thread</span></div>
              <div class="connected-case">
                <header><span>Case 024</span><strong>Kitchen leak</strong><i>In progress</i></header>
                <ol>
                  <li data-state="done"><time>22:14</time><span><strong>Report understood</strong><small>Questions + evidence complete</small></span></li>
                  <li data-state="done"><time>22:20</time><span><strong>Policy checked</strong><small>Approval route identified</small></span></li>
                  <li data-state="active"><time>22:23</time><span><strong>Decision requested</strong><small>Manager sees the full case</small></span></li>
                  <li><time>Next</time><span><strong>Contractor + schedule</strong><small>Prepared to continue</small></span></li>
                </ol>
              </div>
              <p>The team enters when judgment is required, with the context already assembled.</p>
            </section>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="outcome-panel" id="outcome-panel-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="outcome-tab-1" hidden>
          <header><span>Illustrative after-hours intake</span><h3>A complete first response can begin before the desk opens.</h3></header>
          <div class="response-sequence">
            <section class="response-clock">
              <p>Report arrives</p>
              <strong>22:14</strong>
              <span>Resident uses their normal channel</span>
            </section>
            <ol class="response-events">
              <li><time>22:14</time><span><strong>Request acknowledged</strong><small>The resident knows the report is being handled.</small></span></li>
              <li><time>22:15</time><span><strong>Diagnostic questions sent</strong><small>Symptoms, risk, evidence and access.</small></span></li>
              <li><time>22:19</time><span><strong>Initial brief complete</strong><small>Urgency and likely trade proposed.</small></span></li>
              <li><time>22:20</time><span><strong>Human boundary checked</strong><small>Emergency, uncertainty and approval rules applied.</small></span></li>
            </ol>
            <section class="response-handoff">
              <p>What the coordinator receives</p>
              <h4>A decision-ready case, not a missed call.</h4>
              <ul>
                <li>Resident answers</li>
                <li>Media evidence</li>
                <li>Urgency rationale</li>
                <li>Policy checkpoint</li>
                <li>Proposed next move</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="outcome-panel" id="outcome-panel-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="outcome-tab-2" hidden>
          <header><span>Clear system boundary</span><h3>Austi coordinates the work. Your PMS keeps the record.</h3></header>
          <div class="system-boundary">
            <section class="coordination-layer">
              <div class="boundary-title"><span>Austi</span><strong>Operational coordination</strong></div>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Conversation</strong><span>Questions and updates</span></li>
                <li><strong>Decision route</strong><span>Rules and approvals</span></li>
                <li><strong>People</strong><span>Resident, manager, contractor</span></li>
                <li><strong>Progress</strong><span>Follow-up and closure</span></li>
              </ul>
            </section>
            <div class="boundary-transfer" aria-hidden="true"><span>Complete case</span><i></i></div>
            <section class="record-layer">
              <div class="boundary-title"><span>Your PMS</span><strong>Source of truth</strong></div>
              <dl>
                <div><dt>Case summary</dt><dd>Prepared</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Decision history</dt><dd>Attached</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Appointment</dt><dd>Recorded</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Completion evidence</dt><dd>Attached</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Invoice details</dt><dd>Ready</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <p>Exact integration and write-back are defined with the operator’s existing setup.</p>
            </section>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
